Subject: amd64: shifts do not reliably set the zero flag
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Base: c0818978acec60ebb6167fade60fb7012cbf20ca

An x86 shift by a count that masks to zero leaves the flags unchanged,
so jnz (and sel) cannot reuse the flags of a shift that defines its
argument: with %c = 0 the branch below tested the flags of the and.

	%c =w and %n, 63
	%x =l shr -128, %c
	jnz %x, @yes, @no

Do not mark sar, shr and shl as setting the zero flag. Regression:
filnix nanofil/tests/qbe-bugs/jnz-shift-flags.ssa.

